 Leadership, Members & Fellows - The Trilateral Commission 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 About About Us Leadership,
566	672	The Trilateral Commission consists of three main regional groups: North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific.
673	760	The leadership in each consists of a Chairman, Deputy Chairmen, and Executive Director.
761	837	The Commission also has an Executive Committee consisting of 74 members.  
 
837	972	When the Trilateral Commission was first launched, the intention was to have an equal number of members from each of the three regions.
973	1046	The numbers soon began to grow, and ceilings were imposed by around 1980.
1047	1156	These ceilings have been raised somewhat since then as new countries came to be represented in the groups. 
 
1156	1240	The North America Group includes members from Canada, the United States, and Mexico.
1241	1274	It has a total of 135 members. 
 
1274	1593	The European Group includes members from Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Croatia, Cyprus, Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg,  Netherla
1594	1627	It has a total of 184 members. 
 
1627	1788	The Asia Pacific Group includes members from Australia, China, India, Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia, New Zealand, Philippines, Singapore, South Korea, and Thailand.
1789	1821	It has a total of 96 members. 
 
1821	1945	To help preserve the Commission’s unofficial charter, members who enter into government role must rotate off the Commission.
1946	1980	New members are selected annually.
1981	2052	The procedures for rotation and recruitment vary by national group.  
 
2052	2209	In recognition of the Trilateral Commission’s founder, David Rockefeller, all three regional groups also have a David Rockefeller Fellows (DRFs) program.  
 
2209	2289	Our global members represent countries for which there is no national group.  
 
2289	2364	Learn more about our current members, DRFs, and global members below. 
 
  
